WEBVTT

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:05.440
<i>The day that Monroe-senpai and 
Sakura-senpai gave us the shocking news,</i>

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.150
<i>we had a discussion with Ino-senpai, 
who was now our new club president.</i>

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.110
<i>I became the vice president, 
while Ao became the treasurer.</i>

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.110
President

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.110
Inose Mai

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.110
Vice President

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.110
Konohata Mira

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.110
Treasurer

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.110
Manaka Ao

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.470
<i>Our lives at Hoshizaki High 
School were back to normal.</i>

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.490
<i>The only real difference was that, 
several days ago...</i>

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.540
<b>Newspaper Club</b>

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.540
<b>New Members
 Welcome!</b>

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.540
Coming!

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.990
Huh? Student Council President?

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.080
Excuse me.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.510
Who wrote this article on the koi?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.470
Th-That was me.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.180
<i>Apparently, my sister was the one 
who named the koi in the inner garden.</i>

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.930
<b>The koi were named by 
the student council president!</b>

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.000
<i>Rumors of the newspaper with that 
article spread by word of mouth,</i>

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.440
Sold Out

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.440
<i>and their latest issue sold out in a flash.</i>

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.780
<i>Eve-senpai was shouting for joy.</i>

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.480
We've got it pretty clean now.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.430
Yeah.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.720
Hello! It's Suzuya!

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:57.990
Oh, Suzu-chan.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.680
Here. It's the invoice 
for the cultural festival.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.210
Oh, okay.

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.080
I'm so glad you're doing 
well again, Suzu-chan.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.120
As the mascot of the Suzuya Bakery,

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.210
I can't let little things 
like that get me down!

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.190
<i>Unfortunately, the pancakes 
Suzu-chan produced for our club</i>

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:17.470
Food 
Stall 
Contest

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.740
<i>got second place in the cultural 
festival's food stall contest.</i>

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:26.520
Losing was a shock, but I don't 
have time to stay beaten down.

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:29.980
Um, Suzu-san, this is over our budget.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.440
From now on, I'm going on the offensive!

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.400
<i>Suzu-chan is now burning with the 
desire to defeat the manga club.</i>

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.920
<i>Among all this, the only ones who hadn't 
gone back to their normal lives were...</i>

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.410
Good work, everyone.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.360
Oh, Monroe-senpai, Sakura-senpai.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.000
We came by to pick up the 
reference books we left behind.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:51.750
You haven't messed with my stuff, have you?

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.830
Sakura-senpai!

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.760
President

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.760
I'm sorry for suddenly leaving 
you to be club president,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.280
but you don't need to worry so much about it.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.520
But I'm not suited to it at all.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.470
My hands are always full 
just worrying about myself...

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:14.620
Ino-chan, when you're in a bind, you should 
change the way you look at things.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:15.650
Like how?

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.260
When you're club president, you can use 
everyone else as an extension of yourself.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.410
Is that how you saw it?

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.040
Hey.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.290
Sensei? Do you need something?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.750
<b>Request to be an instructor
 on astronomical observation</b>

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:30.750
We got a request from the 
neighborhood kids' group.

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:34.050
A request to be an instructor 
on astronomical observation?

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.060
Some people who saw your exhibit at 
the cultural festival reached out to us.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.970
You don't have to accept if it's 
too last-minute, of course.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.370
What do you think?

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.430
Ino-senpai! I want to do it!

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.150
But Sakura-chan and I have mock exams 
that day, so we can't be there.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:54.980
That's okay! We'll do it with 
just the three of us! Right?!

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:55.990
Wait, Mira!

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:56.980
Wh-What?

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:00.480
We shouldn't try to host an event 
while Ino-senpai's all flustered.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.840
That's why we should accept it.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.630
We can take a leading role in an astronomy 
event, and if it goes well...

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:13.330
I see. That might build Ino-senpai's 
confidence as club president.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:14.530
Right!

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.090
Wait. Suzu-chan, are you planning to come?

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:22.220
I'm on the offensive! 
I'll happily do some night marketing!

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.560
A-All right, then. We'll accept!

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.810
Our new earth sciences club is taking action!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.980
President

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.980
Inose Mai

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.980
Vice President

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.980
Konohata Mira

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.980
Treasurer

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.980
Manaka Ao

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:10.450
07.   The Starry Sky Is a Time Machine

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:12.910
Considering the height of most kids, 
we won't need to extend the tripod.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.620
Will this work for the eyepiece?

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.340
South is that way, so...

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.800
around here?

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.770
I'm sorry I'm not much help.

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:32.950
That's not true at all!

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:38.020
You have the important job of 
taking photos for our newsletter!

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.670
Y-You're right!

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:41.820
I'll do my best!

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.530
Hey, are you all ready?

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.090
The kids will be here soon.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.930
We're all set!

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.870
I'm so nervous.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.140
N-Nice to meet you.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:02.590
We're Hoshizaki High School's 
earth sciences club. So, uh...

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.390
Tonight we'll be using a telescope 
so we can all view the stars.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.340
I see you, squid alien!

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.230
You won't get away with this!

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.560
They're not listening at all.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.010
Then I'll be the squid alien!

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:16.680
Hey, everyone, we're about to 
talk about something important!

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.230
Bathroom...

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.650
Yikes! Hurry!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.990
D-Does anyone else need to go?

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:26.320
Ow! Hiro-kun stepped on my foot!

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.860
Sorry for the wait.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.450
Oh, Suzu-chan, Megu-chan!

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.200
Okay, everyone, pay attention!

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.660
We have star cookies!

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:40.620
Can you pay attention to what these 
ladies have to say while you eat these?

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.840
Okay, go for it.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.130
Thank you!

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:46.340
We appreciate it!

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.510
Nine 
Earths!

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.510
Saturn

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.540
So, today we'll start by looking at

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.510
this planet through the telescope.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.060
I know that one! Saturn!

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.220
Bingo!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:01.100
Saturn is another planet that orbits 
around the Sun, just like Earth.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.840
This is a picture of Earth.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.600
It's so tiny!

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.730
That's just how much bigger Saturn is.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.270
Saturn is roughly the size of nine Earths.

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:14.830
It's surrounded by large, hula-hoop-like 
rings made of ice and rock.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.770
I'm good at the hula hoop!

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.710
Me, too!

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:19.330
Where's Saturn?

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.520
Who here wants to see Saturn?

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:22.790
Me!

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.750
Then why don't we take a look at it now?

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:29.150
Look through here.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:32.340
The telescope can be moved out of place,
 so don't touch here, okay?

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.510
Wow, it's so tiny.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.260
Is it really bigger than Earth?

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:40.980
Yes, it is.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:45.790
But inside, it's actually all empty.
It's said that it could even float on water.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:46.800
I want to see, too!

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:47.660
Me, too!

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:49.320
Yes, yes, one at a time!

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.620
They're getting into it now.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:53.280
Looks like they're having fun.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:55.560
Okay, who's up next?

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:01.160
Well? Were you able to get 
a good look at Saturn?

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:04.020
Yes. It looked the same as 
it did in my field guide.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:04.680
Huh?

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:06.400
What's next?

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.300
Oh, right. Uh...

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.420
Sensei, have some tea.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.540
Oh, thank you.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:13.450
Next we'll have a look at M31,

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:16.010
the galaxy within the 
Andromeda constellation.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.010
Andromeda 
Galaxy

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:22.170
A galaxy is a cluster of many different stars, 
so you can see it clearly through a telescope.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:27.740
Take a look. It's different from the last one.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:30.680
Well?

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.030
It's just some fog.

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:37.280
There's one girl here 
who's proving difficult...

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:44.310
Let's try looking for stars you 
can see with your own eyes.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:45.710
That star is Vega.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.470
That star is Altair, and that star is Deneb.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:53.290
The three of them form the constellation 
known as the Summer Triangle.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:56.880
Wow, you can see summer 
stars in the fall, too?

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.430
I found the triangle!

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.180
No way! Where, where?!

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.320
In the fall, there's also 
the square of Pegasus,

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:07.120
but it's harder to see since its stars 
are darker than the Summer Triangle's.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:09.410
Well, it's not like everyone's going 
to take an interest in it that easily.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.230
I found the triangle!

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.230
Yeah.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:12.540
Lady, I found it!

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.100
Oh, okay!

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.080
U-Um...

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.040
Are you not enjoying the stargazing, uh...

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.500
Haruka

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:23.500
Haruka-chan?

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.730
I didn't want to come 
here in the first place.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.210
There's no one here I get along with.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.920
But my mom told me to come.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.880
What's so fun about looking at stars?

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:38.940
They're all just shining dots to me.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:43.560
Yeah, they are just shining dots in the sky.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:48.770
But look. See how those stars form a 
"W" when you look at them together?

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.770
That's the constellation known as Cassiopeia.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.620
Oh...

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:56.890
Also, a spectral analysis on 
the light from a star can tell you

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:59.510
its surface temperature and 
the elements it's composed of.

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:00.920
Looking at distant stars gives us

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.300
an idea of what our universe 
was like in the distant past.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.540
Sorry, I'm not good at explaining.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.420
The universe of the distant past?

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:14.410
Oh, well, it takes a long time for the 
light of the stars to reach Earth.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:18.380
So, for example, the view we see of Saturn 
is how it looked roughly 80 minutes ago.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.800
The Andromeda Galaxy is even farther away,

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:25.600
so we see how it looked 2.3 million years ago.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:30.460
Then what if you look at a star 
that's even further away?

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:34.570
Well, you might see how the universe 
looked at the very beginning.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:37.360
They may just be glowing dots in the sky,

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.440
but connecting them makes constellations,

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:41.860
and looking at distant ones 
is like using a time machine.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:44.410
Don't you think that's incredible?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.870
There are people studying 
them for just that reason.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:49.420
Excuse me for a moment.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.290
I'm going to go look at that fog again!

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:59.260
So this is what it looked 
like 2.3 million years ago...

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:02.760
Hey, lady, look at this! 
There's a weird shooting star!

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.760
A weird... Oh!

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.970
That's an artificial satellite.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.520
An artificial satellite?! Cool!

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:12.970
You can see it because it's reflecting 
the light of the sun.

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.490
You see lots of them pass 
by while stargazing. It's fun.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:16.940
Wow!

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:23.490
Oh, right, tonight's the best 
night to see the Orionids!

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.730
You'll be likely to see shooting 
stars until tomorrow morning,

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:28.240
so try observing the sky.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.460
Our landmark, Orion, looks...

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.010
like this!

00:11:32.010 --> 00:11:34.500
They'll fly in all directions from here.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.630
They all have great smiles.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:43.090
Yes, they really do.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.860
You can take your time thinking it over, okay?

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:52.260
You can worry and have fun 
along the way as you gradually

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:55.220
work toward being the kind of 
club president only you can be.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:57.370
Right.

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:05.620
Now, it's about time for me to 
seriously start pursuing my dream!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.590
Huh? Your dream?

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:09.200
Huh? Didn't I ever tell you?

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:14.390
My dream is to make Suzuya into 
the world's top bakery company.

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:19.380
I want to open cafés where you can enjoy 
Suzuya's delicious bread throughout the world.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.240
That's an incredibly grand dream.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.220
So, starting now, I'm going 
to do a bit more marketing.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:27.690
Good evening.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:31.240
Oh, I thought I recognized 
your face, Moe-Moe-chan.

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:32.820
Thank you for visiting so often.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:34.380
<i>I'm impressed, Onee.</i>

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.560
<i>I need to get into high school first!</i>

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.780
Good work, girls.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.990
Sensei told me that everyone 
loved the viewing party.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.700
Sakura-senpai!

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:52.080
They're all blurry...

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:02.920
There's Orion!

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:06.290
<i>They may just be glowing dots in the sky,</i>

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.330
<i>but connecting them makes constellations,</i>

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.390
<i>and looking at distant ones 
is like using a time machine.</i>

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.730
Ao, got a second?

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.400
Oh, another one passed by.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:21.780
Did you see it?

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:23.260
Yeah.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.570
Hey, if we could travel through time,
what do you think

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:31.030
<b>Asteroid
 Hunter</b>

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:29.630
<i>we'd be like in the future?</i>

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:35.350
I hope we've discovered an 
asteroid together by then.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:38.000
Yeah.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.160
Ao!

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:47.530
Let's get lunch together!

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.760
Huh? She's not here.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.180
Manaka-san's absent today.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:52.720
Huh?

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.520
Really? That's unusual.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.690
Sensei said she wasn't feeling well.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.610
Suzu-chan...

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:03.310
She was fine when I was with her 
last night, but now she's absent?!

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:05.900
G-Get your thoughts straight
before you yell at me!

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:08.860
Earth Sciences Club

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:08.860
You think it's your fault 
she's not feeling well?

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:09.970
Yeah.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:11.580
What do you mean?

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:16.250
We were watching the Orionids 
together on the phone all night...

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:20.800
But you seem like you're perfectly fine.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.090
I was up to my neck in the kotatsu.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:26.400
Looks like your laziness paid off.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:27.550
Um, Mira-chan...

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:31.400
If you like, why don't we 
go visit her after school?

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.550
Visit her?

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:36.720
I-I'm worried about Ao-san 
as the club president, too,

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:40.090
but if you really are 
the reason she got sick,

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:44.220
it's partially my fault for not managing 
our extracurricular activities well.

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:46.810
So, well... I'd like to apologize with you.

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:50.160
It's our first joint task as 
president and vice president!

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.980
Stop, stop!

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:55.320
You visit the sick because you 
want them to feel better, right?

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:59.510
Do you think she'd be happy to have two 
of her friends bowing their heads to her?

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:01.060
You have a point.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:05.090
I need to go help out at home, 
so I'll give you some advice instead.

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:10.660
"A hundred sweet pick-up lines
that women will love"?

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.220
Just try it! Trust me!

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.060
Yes, welcome.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:17.970
Come on in.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.090
Good evening.

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:22.540
Pardon us. How is Ao-san doing?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.290
She's fine. It's just a cold.

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.140
Maybe the long bath wasn't a good idea...

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:29.240
Sorry to make you worry.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:32.660
Thank goodness. You look 
better than I expected.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.430
Yeah, since I was able to rest all day.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:39.660
Feel better! 
Suzu

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.660
Here's some pudding we got 
from Suzu-san's place.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.370
Wow, thank you!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.880
Also, ahem...

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:52.340
"You are my sun. I-I want you to get 
better soon and light up my heart again."

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:57.510
Suzu-chan's a liar!

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:01.230
I see.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:05.840
In terms of being sweet, desserts 
are better than pick-up lines.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.160
Ino-senpai, what's that?

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:10.190
A memo book I got from Suzu-san.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:14.940
She asked me to take notes on anything 
interesting that happens during our visit.

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.420
It's an important duty!

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.580
Confiscating.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:20.260
Give that back!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:21.760
Still, you surprised me after how 
well you were doing yesterday.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:24.850
I was so worried that our 
phone call was the cause.

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:27.700
No, I handle cold temperatures well.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:31.420
That reminds me, your mother said 
something about a long bath.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:33.930
Were you thinking about something?

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.510
Oh, uh...

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:38.690
Yeah. I was thinking about this book.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:42.220
Is that the asteroid book 
you mentioned earlier?

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:45.230
Yeah. It's an old book I 
found online a while ago.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:48.690
It's the personal experiences of people 
who discovered asteroids, right?

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.000
Yeah.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.700
Is it something that rare?

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:53.500
Yes.

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:57.220
There are plenty of books that 
introduce the asteroids,

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:00.660
but hardly any books discuss the 
actual process of discovering one.

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:03.080
Ao, can I borrow this book?

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.520
Of course. I was planning to lend it to you.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.720
Thanks!

00:17:08.350 --> 00:17:12.460
Wow, this person discovered 
over 800 asteroids!

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:17.520
Sorry we're having all the fun 
when we came to check on you.

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:21.060
No, not at all. I'm having fun, too.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.650
You're sure it's okay?

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:23.220
Huh?

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:24.950
Oh, yes.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:27.730
My fever's down, so I should 
be back at school tomorrow.

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:31.190
I see. That's good.

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.120
Please take care of yourself.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.650
Well, see you at school!

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:38.480
Yeah, thanks.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:46.660
Ao's all better!

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.160
Thank goodness!

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:52.240
Yesterday Mira just kept crying and 
crying, and we couldn't do anything!

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:53.760
Hey, Suzu-chan!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:57.720
That weird advice you gave us 
yesterday went terribly!

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:00.430
You were toying with me, weren't you?!

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:03.840
Well, you're just so honest and cute.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:04.750
Ao-san.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.940
I know we're not very reliable,

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:11.060
but we'll do our best as 
president and vice president.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.470
So if you ever need anything, please tell us.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:17.030
Thank you.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.210
It was super embarrassing!

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:21.030
I get it already! I give, I give!

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.260
What's the fuss today?

00:18:24.400 --> 00:18:26.620
Monroe-senpai!

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:31.500
Techniques for
 photographing stars

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:31.500
<b>Taking Starry Sky Photos</b>

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:31.500
<b>Photographing celestial bodies 
with digital cameras</b>

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:31.500
I wonder if the photos from the viewing party 
were blurry because of the shutter speed.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:35.830
I thought I'd take them without the flash, 
but I guess I adjusted it too much.

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:38.760
I tried taking some more after 
resetting the settings, but...

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:41.220
They're still blurry.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:44.740
Maybe you're not half-pressing the button?

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:45.920
Half-pressing?

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:49.830
You press the shutter button 
down halfway to focus.

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.940
I see! I'll give it a try right away!

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.040
There!

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.860
Yeah, more and more causes 
are revealing themselves...

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:01.670
I guess I can't just take 
them with my smartphone.

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:03.280
That's not true.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:05.600
Sometimes it's better to do what's familiar

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:08.520
than to force yourself to try something new.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:10.580
Hey, listen to this! I got the recommendation!

00:19:11.990 --> 00:19:15.000
If it comes down to it, you can 
tweak it with retouch software.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:17.760
I don't know what you two are talking about,

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:20.510
You can brighten Sakura-chan's 
skin and make her eyes bigger.

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:20.510
but I can tell you're fooling around with me.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:22.470
You got the recommendation slot?!

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:27.280
The notice just reached my house.
My mom sent me a text about it.

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:29.730
Congratulations, Sakura-senpai!

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.570
Congratulations!

00:19:32.390 --> 00:19:34.240
Congratulations, Sakura-chan!

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:35.540
Thanks.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:38.080
You should be getting yours, 
too, if I got mine.

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:39.900
Yeah, it should be there.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:41.050
Huh?

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:43.990
We both applied for recommendation 
to the same university.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:46.320
We're in different majors, though.

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:49.480
We decided to keep quiet about 
it until exams were over,

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:52.250
since we didn't want to make you all worry.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:52.870
Hey!

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:57.000
Quit talking about useless stuff 
and hurry home to check for yours!

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.030
Okay.

00:19:58.030 --> 00:19:59.960
I'll text you when I find out.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.020
I'll see you all tomorrow!

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:04.680
<i>The text from Monroe-senpai...</i>

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.040
<i>never came, even by the next day.</i>

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.760
Inbox

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.760
Email Search

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.760
No new messages

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:09.890
I-I'm so curious.

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:13.100
Class 1-3

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:13.100
Mira? It's almost time for homeroom to start.

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:15.580
Huh? Ino-senpai?

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:17.400
Mira-chan! Ao-san!

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:19.360
Huh? Ao?

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:22.790
It looks like she's not in her classroom yet.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.020
I'm getting even more worried.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:30.790
Class 3-1

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.250
<b>Earth Sciences Club</b>

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:35.640
This is why we didn't tell 
you all about the exams.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:40.460
We couldn't stand to watch you 
get this flustered over us.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:41.560
But, but...

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:43.150
No buts!

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:44.720
There are still more exams,

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:47.530
so make sure you don't let 
Monroe see you looking like that!

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:48.510
O-Okay.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:52.890
There's not much we can do 
about this for her, anyway.

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:56.740
So instead, focus on keeping 
a handle on yourselves.

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:57.270
Got it?

00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:58.780
Yes.

00:20:58.780 --> 00:20:59.660
That's it!

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:06.240
Though I did get a bit too 
carried away yesterday...

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:12.720
Ao! Let's try organizing the information 
we have on asteroids thus far!

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.050
S-Sure.

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:20.420
<i>What I should be doing right now...</i>

00:21:24.710 --> 00:21:26.450
<i>Earth Science Olympiad?</i>

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:32.570
<i>This is my first step toward becoming 
an independent club president!</i>

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:35.310
<i>Sometimes it's better to do what's familiar</i>

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:38.100
<i>than to force yourself to try something new.</i>

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:42.070
<i>I can't just indulge in their kindness!</i>

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:44.110
Endou-sensei!

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:46.650
Oh, Inose. What is it?

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:51.620
Um, do we still have time to apply 
for this earth sciences competition?

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:55.710
<i>We're going to keep moving forward.</i>

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:59.040
<i>Because even if some things 
don't go the way we hope,</i>

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:03.660
<i>we have faith that a 
wonderful future awaits us.</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.020
08. 
Winter Diamond

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:38.910
Next time, "Winter Diamond."
